+# Lose sight of a difference, then find it again
+
+25 September 2026. The paired study already has a strong storage experiment. The new encounter makes its spatial receiver legible through walking: your depth between A and B selects the same section of both. Gold frames mark that plane; the existing floor and wall textures show it.
+
+At the beginning, address (5,5,5) is the only intervention. Walk beyond its slice and the selected difference image is blank, although the field has not changed. Return and it reappears. Compare this with INTEGER storage removing the uniform unforced intervention on the first update. A disappearance from view and a disappearance from stored state require different accounts.
+
+Keep all five existing works, the paired model, source equation excerpts and mature manuscript argument. Add only the early walking encounter and its native photograph. Correct the stale companion claim that CA_AgentsCircuits is off route; the active sequence already places it directly before this hall.
+
+Native evidence and exact revisions: doc/book/iterations/2026-09-25-ca-walking-slice/. Desktop checks do not establish headset comfort, Quest performance or learner understanding.
